        {
          "name": "fee_destination",
          "docs": [
            "The claimer's ASSOCIATED token account, and only that one.",
            "",
            "This used to check the owner rather than the address, so that a",
            "destination could be an ATA or not. That was too loose, and the reason",
            "is a seam this program cannot see. When `fee_claimer` is a peard",
            "market, that program credits holders by reading its reward vault,",
            "which it derives as the ATA. Fees claimed into some other account the",
            "market happens to own would satisfy the old check, arrive somewhere",
            "real, and then be creditable by nothing and recoverable by nobody.",
            "",
            "The ATA is derivable by anyone from the mint and the owner, so",
            "requiring it costs a caller nothing and removes a way to strand money",
            "that no error would ever have reported."
          ],
          "writable": true,
          "pda": {
