    {
      "name": "migrate_pool",
      "docs": [
        "Name the warehouse standing behind this pool's quote leg. Once.",
        "",
        "The point is that somebody reading the POOL sees the backing, rather",
        "than having to know a second program exists and which account in it to",
        "look up. A backing you have to be told about is one most people never",
        "check.",
        "",
        "Verified rather than trusted. The reserve is read by hand with the",
        "peard_vault program pinned by the caller-supplied id checked against the",
        "account's owner, its discriminator checked because owner and length",
        "are not a type, and then the only check that makes it MEAN anything:",
        "that reserve's own `receipt_mint` must be this pool's quote mint. A",
        "pool cannot claim a warehouse that does not issue the token it trades.",
        "",
        "One way, like `fee_claimer`. A backing somebody can repoint is a story.",
        "Grow a pool written before `backing_reserve` existed.",
        "",
        "The pool PDA is seeded on the base mint, so a pool can never be",
        "re-created: without this, every pool already on chain stops",
        "deserialising the moment the deployed program carries the larger",
        "struct, and there is no other repair path. Mirrors peard_perps's",
        "`migrate_market`, which exists for exactly the same reason.",
        "",
        "Permissionless and idempotent. `realloc` with `zero_init` leaves the",
        "existing bytes alone and zeroes only the new tail, and zero is",
        "`Pubkey::default()`, which is precisely \"nothing backs this pool\". A",
        "migrated pool therefore behaves exactly as it did before."
      ],
